<h1 id="anexo-ii-condiciones-específicas-del-nivel-desarrollador"><strong>Annex II – Specific Conditions of the Developer Level </strong></h1>
<details>
<summary>See Annex II </summary>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p><strong>Applicability </strong></p>
<p>This annex will apply when the Adhering Entity has signed the Framework Contract and obtains
                the qualification to hold the Developer Participation Level in the ISBE network,
                conformity with the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>and the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>.
            </p>
<p>The eventual accumulation of this Level of Participation with other Levels of Participation will be governed
                so they foresee the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>and the rest
                of ISBE policies, particularly regarding functional segregation, conflicts of interest and
                node operation. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Purpose of the annex </strong></p>
<p>The purpose of this annex will be to establish the particular conditions under which the
                Adherent Entity plays the Developer Participation Level, understood as the role that
                enables you to design, develop, deploy and maintain Use Cases and <em>Smart Contracts </em>about
                ISBE networks, as well as to offer services based on said infrastructure, all in the
                terms provided in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and in the rest of
                ISBE policies that are applicable. </p>
<p>This Level of Participation will not enable the Adhering Entity to operate nodes of the ISBE network; the
                Node operation will require, where appropriate, the assumption of specific Node Operator levels.
                of Execution and/or Consensus Node Operator through the corresponding annexes. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Access and qualification requirements as a Developer </strong></p>
<p>In order for the Adhering Entity to hold the Developer Participation Level, it must, in
                all times: </p>
<ol type="a">
<li>
<p>Comply with the general requirements for admission, permanence and updating of information
                        established in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Accredit sufficient technical and organizational capacity to design, develop, deploy and
                        maintain Use Cases and <em>Smart Contracts </em>according to the criteria of the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>, taking into account
                        takes into account, where appropriate, the risk assessment criteria applied by the Management Entity of
                        in accordance with its internal risk management policies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Overcome the evaluation, approval and, where appropriate, technical and quality audit processes.
                        cybersecurity that provides for <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Sign this annex, assuming the specific obligations associated with the Level of
                        Developer Participation and committing to adhere to the operational guidelines that
                        The Managing Entity teaches in accordance with the ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>The Managing Entity may deny or revoke the qualification as a Developer when they do not comply or
                these requirements are no longer met, in accordance with the Framework Contract, the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>and the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>.
            </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Functional capabilities of the Developer Level </strong></p>
<p>In its capacity as Developer, the Adhering Entity may, in the terms and with the limits
                established in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and the <strong>ECO1030 Policy – ​​SCs pausing/locking/data deletion policy </strong>.:
            </p>
<ol type="a">
<li>
<p>Design and propose Use Cases for deployment on ISBE networks, subjecting them to the
                        evaluation, prioritization and approval procedures established by the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Deploy <em>Smart Contracts </em>using exclusively the means and tools
                        authorized by ISBE, including, in particular: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>the use of
                        assistant or <em>Wizard </em>” no-code and standard libraries <em>Smart Contracts </em>preconfigured and pre-approved by ISBE, which allow the deployment
                        of contracts based on standard templates without the need for programming, under the workflows
                        control defined in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>; and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>the deployment of the Developer's own developments that have
                        previously passed the conformity or approval test defined in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>, in which
                        They evaluate, among other aspects, security, interoperability, traceability and
                        regulatory adaptation. Only the <em>Smart Contracts </em>who have satisfactorily passed
                        said conformity test may be authorized to operate on the ISBE network and be managed
                        through the corresponding Factory Contracts. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Consume the infrastructure and Blockchain-as-a-Service (BaaS) services that ISBE makes available
                        available to the Developers or, where appropriate, provided through Node Operators
                        of Execution, in the terms that provide for the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and the <strong>Policy INF1050 – Digital identities, credentials and management policy
                            access </strong>, without this implying operating its own nodes. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Request, where appropriate, the inclusion of your Use Cases and the associated services in the
                        catalog or directory of ISBE solutions, in accordance with the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and with the <strong>Policy ADM1010 – Fees and remuneration policy </strong>regarding
                        economic conditions. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Specific obligations of the Developer Level </strong></p>
<p>In addition to the obligations derived from the Framework Contract and the ISBE Policies, the Entity
                Adherent, as a Developer, must: </p>
<ol type="a">
<li>
<p>Strictly comply with the provisions of the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>, the <strong>ECO1030 Policy – ​​SCs pausing/locking/data deletion policy </strong>, in
                        relationship with the life cycle of Use Cases and <em>Smart Contracts </em>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Use exclusively the deployment, update, pause and withdrawal mechanisms of <em>Smart Contracts </em>that foresees the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>, including
                        Factory Contracts and other authorized technical governance components, refraining from
                        deploy or modify code outside of said channels. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Respect the intellectual property obligations and licensing regime provided for in the <strong>Policy NOR1070 – Intellectual Property Policy </strong>, including the rules
                        relating to ownership, licensing, contributions to the ISBE network and use of components
                        common. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Respect the obligations of confidentiality and privacy included in the <strong>Policy NOR1050 – Confidentiality Policy </strong>and in the <strong>Policy NOR1060 – Personal data protection policy </strong>, minimizing the
                        inclusion of personal data in on-chain records and using, to the extent possible,
                        hashing techniques, pseudonymization or other equivalent mechanisms, in accordance with the <strong>ECO1030 Policy – ​​SCs pausing/locking/data deletion policy </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Comply with the rules of neutrality, fair competition and prevention of conflicts of interest
                        established in the <strong>Policy NOR1040 – Conflict of Interest Policy </strong>and in
                        the <strong>Policy NOR1080 – Competition and neutrality policy </strong>, especially
                        when offering services to third parties on the ISBE infrastructure. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Provide the Managing Entity with the information reasonably necessary so that it can
                        evaluate risks, incidents and compliance with ISBE Policies in relation to the Cases
                        of Use and <em>Smart Contracts </em>deployed, and collaborate in the review or
                        audit that, if applicable, is carried out on said Use Cases. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Assume, in the scope of Use Cases and <em>Smart Contracts </em>that develops or
                        deployment, full responsibility for its life cycle, security of services
                        associated and the legal implications derived from its use, guaranteeing compliance
                        of the obligations that apply to you in terms of data protection, property
                        intellectual, cybersecurity and sector regulations. To this end, it will implement procedures for
                        identification and due diligence (including, where applicable, KYB/KYC/AML checks)
                        appropriate to the nature of the services provided and the end users, in accordance
                        with applicable regulations and ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Maintain, when the nature of the Use Case requires it to generate transactional activity
                        relevant information, access to critical functionalities or potential exposure to regulatory risks, a
                        registration <em>off-chain </em>, verifiable, provided and updated from end users
                        that interact with the deployed services, with the scope provided in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and without prejudice
                        of the provisions of the Policy <strong>NOR1060 – Personal data protection policy </strong>regarding the data
                        that, where appropriate, are incorporated into said registry. This record will have traceability purposes
                        and reinforcement of the responsibility of the issuer and will not in itself constitute a complete system
                        compliance in matters of prevention of money laundering or financing of
                        terrorism. It may be subject to review or audit, upon reasoned request, by
                        the Managing Entity or the competent authority, especially in the event of an incident of
                        security or investigation of possible breaches. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Diligently monitor vulnerabilities, incidents and anomalies associated with the
                        Use Cases and <em>Smart Contracts </em>under your control, as well as integrations, APIs and
                        related bookstores, responding without undue delay to incidents that occur
                        and applying the updates, corrections and improvements that are necessary or that are
                        indicated by the Managing Entity or by the ISBE Policies, in order to maintain a level of
                        safety and quality aligned with the standards required in the ISBE network. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Economic conditions </strong></p>
<p>The rates, fees, quotas, compensation or any other economic conditions associated with the
                Developer Participation Level, including service consumption <em>Blockchain-as-a-Service </em>(BaaS), the use of advanced tools or the inclusion of services
                in catalogues, will be governed entirely by what is established by the <strong>Policy ADM1010 – Fees and remuneration policy </strong>, in its current version in
                every moment. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Developer Level Completion </strong></p>
<p>Voluntary withdrawal, revocation or any other form of termination of the Participation Level of
                Developer will be governed by the provisions of the Framework Contract and the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>, without
                prejudice to the fact that the operational consequences on the Use Cases and <em>Smart Contracts </em>deployed (including pausing, blocking, migrating or retiring) are
                conform to the provisions of the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and in the <strong>ECO1030 Policy – ​​SCs pausing/locking/data deletion policy </strong>.
            </p>
</li>
